WEBVTT

00:01:58.808 --> 00:02:00.473
that those surfaces reflect.

00:02:00.497 --> 00:02:04.880
Now, can any of you see the predator
that's about to jump out at you?

00:02:04.904 --> 00:02:07.928
And if you haven't seen it yet,
you're dead, right?

00:02:07.952 --> 00:02:08.953
(Laughter)

00:02:08.977 --> 00:02:11.315
Can anyone see it? Anyone? No?

00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:12.808
Now let's see the surfaces

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.686
according to the quality of light
that they reflect.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.251
And now you see it.

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:20.594
So, color enables us to see

00:02:20.618 --> 00:02:23.044
the similarities and differences
between surfaces,

00:02:23.068 --> 00:02:26.114
according to the full spectrum
of light that they reflect.

00:02:26.138 --> 00:02:27.599
But what you've just done

00:02:27.623 --> 00:02:30.663
is in many respects
mathematically impossible.